   "text": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\n`release-notes` drafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags. It groups PRs by Conventional Commit type, with features, fixes, and breaking changes first.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when you need a release notes draft for a tag range. The skill runs only when you invoke it:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nUse `technical-writing` to edit prose. `release-notes` gathers the PRs and drafts the notes.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. Checks that `gh` is signed in. If `gh auth status` fails, it stops.\n2. Checks that both tags exist. If either tag is missing, it stops before drafting with `TAG_UNRESOLVED`.\n3. Gathers merged PRs between the tags and skips PRs labeled `skip-notes`.\n4. Groups the PRs by type. For PRs with multiple type labels, grouping uses a strict-majority rule. Label order breaks ties.\n5. Includes a migration line for each breaking change. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\n## What you get\n\nThe skill writes `RELEASE_NOTES.md` in the working tree and stops. It never publishes.\n\nThe draft includes grouped release notes and marks missing migration guidance for breaking changes.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will it publish a release?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens to a breaking change with no migration note?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
